            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0496" n="402" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg402"/>

                <head>No. 289.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pendleton to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 8, 1887</date>.
                        (Received November 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 534.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith the
                    report of military cases (prepared by Mr. Coleman, secretary of legation), which
                    have required the attention of the legation and been brought to a
                    conclusion.</p>
                <p>The period embraced in this report is from November 2, 1885, to date, and refers
                    to Cases No. 127 to No. 181, inclusive, excepting No. 128, heretofore reported
                    with my dispatch No. 100, of November 2, 1885, and No. 176, which is unfinished.
                    The latter, and one quite recently presented, constitute the only cases now
                    pending.</p>
                <p>It will be remembered that copies of the correspondence in each case as it arose
                    were forwarded <hi rendition="#italic">pari passu</hi>, on the suggestion of the
                    Department.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. H.
                    Pendleton.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d289-a1.xml" xpointer="d289-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
